From: miroe <260228444+boartat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 02:04:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] dxmt: reclaim idle dynamic buffer spares per command queue
 (miroe MUMA v0)

WRITE_DISCARD renames a dynamic buffer to a fresh allocation while the GPU
still reads the old one, and queues the old one as a spare. The queue never
shrinks, and a buffer that is no longer mapped never drops its spares, so a
burst of discards keeps its peak memory for the life of the buffer (DXMT
issue #260). Each command queue now keeps a registry of dynamic buffers with
spares; its finish thread frees spares the GPU has been done with for more
than 300 submissions, every 16 completions. allocate() drains stale spares
the same way. Sequence ids are per queue, so is the registry.

Engine/tests/c/d3d11-memory-test.c on ARM64 Wine + FEX, M4 Pro: GPU memory
after the burst 920 MB -> 312 MB (the buffers' own size), back within ~2 s;
burst throughput unchanged (1.462 vs 1.463 ms/frame).

Source: miroe (Miro project). License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like DXMT.
Written with AI assistance: per DXMT's CONTRIBUTING this is not for an
upstream pull request.
